<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event · disaster</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hurricane Dorian</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">2019</span> · <a href="/centuries/21st-century">21st century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Hurricane Dorian was an Atlantic hurricane that struck the northern Bahamas as a Category 5 storm in September 2019. It stalled over the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abaco-islands">Abaco Islands</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/grand-bahama">Grand Bahama</a> for more than a day, with sustained winds near 185 miles per hour, causing catastrophic storm surges and destruction. It was the worst natural disaster in Bahamian history, leaving dozens dead, many more missing and damage estimated at several billion dollars.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hurricane-dorian.jpg" alt="Hurricane Dorian" width="320" height="386" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: ABI imagery from NOAA'S GOES-16 Satellite · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Dorian_2019-09-01_1641Z.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
